Chapter: DiskFactsMbrGuard
  cites Kernel chapter DiskFacts
  cites Foreword chapter FactStore
  cites Foreword chapter Hamt
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Foreword chapter Sha256
  cites Foreword chapter FactLog

 The residual case. The first guard looked for "EFI PART" at sector 1, so it
 caught a GPT disk and missed a disk carrying only an MBR partition table --
 which was still written straight through, and its partition table still
 eaten, by a store that believed it had been made safe. A bare FAT volume
 with no partition table at all lands here too: its boot sector ends in the
 same two bytes, and the store overwriting a filesystem is the same damage
 as the store overwriting a partition table.

 The fixture is 32 KB whose sector 0 carries nothing but the 0x55AA boot
 signature and whose sector 1 is filled with a sentinel.

   count  must stay 0, so the refusal happens BEFORE the write and not as a
          report after it.
   sig    sector 0 must still end 85, 170. The superblock the store would
          have written there zeroes the sector, so a store that wrote would
          take these two bytes with it.
   entry  sector 1 must still be the sentinel. This is the sector the
          store's second superblock copy lands on, so it is the one that
          moves if a checkpoint got through when the write did not.

 We say:

Section: Readings

  byte-at : Integer, Integer -> [Device.Block] Integer
  byte-at (sector) (i) = act
    buf <- block-read-sector sector
    peek-byte buf i
  end

Section: Body

  opening : [Console, Device.Block] Nothing
  opening = act
    let store = disk-load
    in let attempted = disk-write-fact store DefinitionFact "hello" 0
    in let flushed = disk-checkpoint attempted
    in act
      lo <- byte-at 0 510
      hi <- byte-at 0 511
      ent <- byte-at 1 0
      print-line-uni ("count " & show (disk-fact-count attempted))
      print-line-uni ("sig " & (if lo == 85 & hi == 170 then "intact" else "GONE"))
      print-line-uni ("entry " & (if ent == 165 then "intact" else "GONE"))
    end
  end
